    "honest_framing": "Wf-131 P3 DEFERRED 7-run sweep MEASURED 7 of 7 (metal, seed) pairs at 50 epochs. Overall mean test_auc = 0.7577 ± 0.0924 (sample std over 7 runs) — PARTIAL KRASNOV PASS: above gate_target=0.7 (PASS), below krasnov_gate_target=0.86 (BELOW with gap −0.102). Per-fold: Rh mean = 0.8798 ± 0.0115 (PASS krasnov 0.86 with margin +0.020), Re mean = 0.7088 ± 0.0482 (BELOW krasnov 0.86 with gap −0.151). Rh fold lift vs R17 = +0.5121 (massive lift; per-seed test_auc values 0.8879 + 0.8717 confirm seed-0=0.274 outlier was structural noise not a real failure mode per Wf-131 P3 §0 honest-negative analysis). Re fold lift vs R17 = +0.2029 (modest lift on smallest cohort n=868 test set). Re seed=4 MEASURED 0.7196 — pulls Re mean up from 0.7061 (6-run) to 0.7088 (7-run). New Re seed=4 is the 2nd-best Re seed, validating that GPU wrapper termination was an orchestration bug not a model quality issue. WARNING: prior `metrics/by_metric/metal_lomo_auc_wasserstein.json` aggregate was WRONG (n=1, value=0.7196 = Re seed=4 only, written at Re seed=4 completion 16:44:58 by `wf125_p2 :: wrote metrics/by_metric/metal_lomo_auc_wasserstein.json` per run.log tail). Corrected aggregate now covers all 7 MEASURED runs with per_fold_auc_mean + per_fold_auc_std + per_run_auc + n_runs=7 + n_folds=2.",
    "wrapper_label_bug_surfaced": "molmetal/reports/wf131_p3_deferred_runs/{Rh/seed3,Rh/seed4,Re/seed0,Re/seed1}/{Rh,Re}/per_seed_metrics.json (wrapper format) had seed-field labels SWAPPED between paired directories — the wrapper write may have over-written the prior directory's per_seed_metrics.json. Flat files per_seed_metrics_seed{n}.json are CANONICAL and labels are correct. aggregate.json files are CONSISTENT. Recommendation: delete or correct the wrapper-format per_seed_metrics.json files; emit only the flat per_seed_metrics_seed{n}.json files going forward.",
